Send the LFG proposal member role as the INDEX the 3.3.5 client expects, not as
AzerothCore's role bitmask.
Touches: src/server/game/Handlers/LFGHandler.cpp, WorldSession::SendLfgUpdateProposal()

Why: players saw this on every dungeon-finder pop, repeatedly, and on accept --

  Interface\FrameXML\LFGFrame.lua:337: Unknown role: UNKNOWN
  ... GetTexCoordsForRole -> LFDDungeonReadyStatus_UpdateIcon
      -> LFDDungeonReadyPopup_Update

-- and separately reported "healers marked as dps". Those are one bug.

THE EVIDENCE, because two earlier fixes were wrong and both were guesses.

FrameXML was extracted from the client's own MPQs rather than recalled:

  * LFGFrame.lua:337 `GetTexCoordsForRole(role)` accepts exactly GUIDE, TANK,
    HEALER, DAMAGER and calls error() on anything else. `role` is a STRING.
  * LFDFrame.lua:675 `LFDDungeonReadyStatus_UpdateIcon` gets it from
    `GetLFGProposalMember(button:GetID())`, and those buttons carry ids 1-5 in
    LFDFrame.xml, so the index is not the problem.
  * `GetLFGProposalMember` returns `isLeader, role, level, responded, accepted,
    name, class` -- isLeader is its OWN return value, so the leader bit never
    belonged in the role field.

That string comes from client C code, so Wow.exe was searched for the table. It
holds exactly one: three pointers at VA 0xad87b0 (file offset 0x6d67b0),
pointing at the strings at 0xa29b70/78/80, in this order:

    index 0 -> "TANK"    index 1 -> "HEALER"    index 2 -> "DAMAGER"

"GUIDE" does not occur in the 3.3.5 binary at all. The client indexes that
table with the number the server sends. AzerothCore sends the bitmask, so what
players actually got was:

    PLAYER_ROLE_TANK   = 2 -> index 2 -> "DAMAGER"  (tank draws the dps icon)
    PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER = 4 -> out of range -> "UNKNOWN" -> Lua error
    PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE = 8 -> out of range -> "UNKNOWN" -> Lua error

Every observation fits: the error fired on every pop no matter what was done to
the mask, its Count tracked the number of non-tank members, only tanks escaped
it (while rendering wrongly), and "healers show as dps" was a separate report of
the same root cause.

WHAT THE TWO EARLIER ATTEMPTS DID, AND WHY THEY MISSED.

Both assumed a bitmask, so both produced values the client still could not read:

  1. Narrowing a multi-bit mask down to a single role bit. Still sent 4 or 8.
  2. Stripping PLAYER_ROLE_LEADER. Turned 9 into 8 -- still out of range.

The clue was sitting in the log the whole time: both patches logged whenever
they corrected a mask, and that line never fired once across a full uptime. The
value on the wire was already a single clean role bit and the client still could
not resolve it, which rules out the mask's SHAPE and points at its MEANING.
"Verify, then theorise" applies to the second guess as much as the first.

The mapping and the fallback are kept: a member arriving with no role bits at
all still goes out as damage rather than as something the client cannot render,
and that case is still logged, because it is a genuine upstream bug (a bot
placed into a group outside the queue, or a proposal formed without
CheckGroupRoles running). What is gone is the pretence that narrowing a mask was
ever going to fix this.

--- a/src/server/game/Handlers/LFGHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Handlers/LFGHandler.cpp
@@ (replacing NarrowProposalRoleForClient)
-static uint8 NarrowProposalRoleForClient(uint8 role)
-{
-    uint8 const leader = role & lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_LEADER;
-    if (role & lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
-        return leader | lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK;
-    ...
-}
+enum LfgClientRoleIndex : uint32
+{
+    LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_TANK   = 0,
+    LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_HEALER = 1,
+    LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_DAMAGE = 2,
+};
+
+static uint32 ProposalRoleIndexForClient(uint8 role)
+{
+    if (role & lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
+        return LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_TANK;
+    if (role & lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER)
+        return LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_HEALER;
+    return LFG_CLIENT_ROLE_DAMAGE;
+}

@@ SendLfgUpdateProposal -- sort by what is actually sent
-        switch (NarrowProposalRoleForClient(player.role) & ~lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_LEADER)
+        switch (ProposalRoleIndexForClient(player.role))

@@ SendLfgUpdateProposal -- the per-member write
-        uint8 const role = NarrowProposalRoleForClient(player.role);
-        ... logging for masks that were never narrowed ...
-        data << uint32(role);                              // Role
+        uint32 const roleIndex = ProposalRoleIndexForClient(player.role);
+        if (!(player.role & (lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK | lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER | lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE)))
+            LOG_ERROR("lfg", "SMSG_LFG_PROPOSAL_UPDATE: proposal {} member [{}] has no LFG role at all (mask {}), sending damage",
+                proposal.id, pguid.ToString(), uint32(player.role));
+        data << uint32(roleIndex);                         // Role INDEX, not a mask
